export const title = "Milestone XProtect Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Milestone XProtect Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3>1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 102700 or later.</li>\n<li>Milestone XProtect 2023 R1 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>There are two ways to integrate AIBridge with the Milestone XProtect VMS:</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1) Case 1</h3>\n<p>AIBridge receives an RTSP video stream from an IP camera, and after AI analysis, provides annotated video along with event data. The annotated video is transcoded by AIBridge's AI analysis to include object recognition info, bounding boxes, zone info, and more.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 340\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"140\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f6cfcf\" stroke=\"#c98a8a\"/>\n  <text x=\"105\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5c2626\" font-weight=\"700\">IP Cameras</text>\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"40\" width=\"190\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"655\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\" font-weight=\"700\">XProtect</text>\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"200\" width=\"190\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3a3f4a\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"655\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">AIBridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <line x1=\"655\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#e07a3f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <text x=\"670\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#e07a3f\">AI Event &amp; Annotated Video</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrM\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Case 1 &#8211; AIBridge provides annotated video and event data directly to XProtect</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2) Case 2</h3>\n<p>Both AIBridge and the Milestone XProtect VMS receive an RTSP video stream from the IP camera at the same time, and AIBridge sends its AI analysis events to the XProtect VMS. AIBridge can also receive its RTSP stream from the Milestone XProtect VMS instead of directly from the IP camera.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 340\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"140\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f6cfcf\" stroke=\"#c98a8a\"/>\n  <text x=\"105\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5c2626\" font-weight=\"700\">IP Cameras</text>\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"40\" width=\"190\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"655\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\" font-weight=\"700\">XProtect</text>\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"200\" width=\"190\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3a3f4a\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"655\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">AIBridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM2)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM2)\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <line x1=\"655\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#e07a3f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM2)\"/>\n  <text x=\"695\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#e07a3f\">AI Event</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrM2\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Case 2 &#8211; AIBridge and XProtect both receive the camera stream directly; only AI events are forwarded</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<h3>2.1 Configure Milestone XProtect VMS</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to integrate AIBridge with the Milestone XProtect VMS using the Case 1 method.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. For a Case 2 integration, you can skip step 1 (Add AIBridge to Milestone XProtect VMS) and start from step 2 (Enable XProtect Analytics Events).</p>\n\n<h4>2.1.1 Add AIBridge to Milestone XProtect VMS</h4>\n<p>In the XProtect Management Client, select <strong>Add Hardware</strong>.</p>\n<p>If you know the AIBridge device's IP address, select <strong>Manual</strong>.</p>\n<p>Enter the AIBridge login credentials.</p>\n<p>For the device driver option, select <strong>ONVIF</strong>.</p>\n<p>Enter the AIBridge IP address. Unless you changed AIBridge's ONVIF service port setting, the port is 80. HTTPS is not used.</p>\n<p>Add the detected AIBridge hardware and rename it as you like. If it fails, double-check the settings and try again.</p>\n\n<h4>2.1.2 Enable XProtect Analytics Events</h4>\n<p>In the XProtect Management Client, click <strong>Tools &gt; Options</strong>.</p>\n<p>On the Analytics Event tab, select the <strong>Enabled</strong> checkbox. The service port must be open on the firewall. If you changed the service port, you must enter the same port number when registering AIBridge's Milestone action handler.</p>\n\n<h4>2.1.3 Add an Analytics Event and Alarm Definition</h4>\n<p>In the left panel of the XProtect Management Client, select <strong>Analytics events</strong>, right-click, and choose <strong>Add New</strong>.</p>\n<p>Enter the event name <strong>AIBridge Event</strong>. This value is the key that distinguishes events between AIBridge and XProtect, and it must also be entered into the <strong>Message key</strong> property of AIBridge's Milestone action handler setting.</p>\n<p>Add an <strong>Alarm definition</strong> in the XProtect Management Client.</p>\n<p>For Trigger Event, select <strong>Analytics Events</strong>, and for Trigger Source select the <strong>AIBridge Event</strong> you added earlier. Add AIBridge's channel to the Trigger Source.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. If you register an IPCAM channel instead of an AIBridge camera channel as the Trigger Source, the integration works as a Case 2 integration.</p>\n\n<h3>2.2 Configure AIBridge</h3>\n<h4>2.2.1 Add a Video Stream</h4>\n<p>Set up (add) a video stream. You can add a video stream by using ONVIF device discovery, or by directly entering the IPCAM's RTSP stream address.</p>\n\n<h4>2.2.2 AI App Settings</h4>\n<p>Select the AI app you want and configure the AI event for that channel.</p>\n<p>AIBridge offers 50+ AI apps. See the app catalog for the full list.</p>\n<p>In the action settings, click the <strong>Add</strong> button to add a Milestone action handler.</p>\n\n<h4>2.2.3 Enter Milestone XProtect VMS Server Info</h4>\n<p>Enter the Milestone XProtect VMS's IP address and Analytic Event service port number, then click the channel <strong>Mapping</strong> button.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>IP Address</span><input value=\"192.168.76.62\" disabled>\n    <span>Service Port</span><input value=\"9090\" disabled>\n    <span>Channel Mapping</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">Mapping</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Enter the Milestone XProtect VMS's camera channel ID.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. If you enter an IPCAM channel ID instead of an AIBridge camera channel ID in the camera mapping info, the integration works as a Case 2 integration.</p>\n<p>Click and hold a channel to view the UUID of the camera channel ID at the bottom of the info tab.</p>\n<p>Enter the name of the <strong>Analytic Event</strong> you added in Milestone XProtect into the <strong>Message key</strong> property. This guide uses <strong>AIBridge Event</strong>.</p>\n<p>The Object field can be used in a number of ways. You can send additional information &#8212; such as event text or LPR info &#8212; to the Milestone XProtect Alarm Manager by entering it here.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. To configure different Object properties for each AI app, you can create a separate Milestone action handler for each AI app.</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Test</strong> button to confirm the Test Event appears in the Milestone XProtect Client.</p>\n<p>Once the event test succeeds, check the <strong>Activate Milestone action handler</strong> checkbox and click <strong>Apply</strong> to save the handler setting.</p>\n<p>Finally, click the <strong>Save</strong> button at the bottom of the AI app settings to save all configuration.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3>3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>In the live view of the XProtect Smart Client, analytics events are listed in the alarm panel and shown on the annotated video.</p>\n\n<h3>3.2 Search</h3>\n<p>In the search menu, click the <strong>Search for...</strong> button and select Alarms to search for AI events.</p>\n\n<h3>3.3 Alarm Manager</h3>\n<p>Clicking an individual alarm in Alarm Manager shows detailed information about when the event occurred, along with the recorded video.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Alarm Manager is supported in Milestone XProtect Express+ and above.</p>\n<p>To show analytics event properties in the Smart Client, you may need to adjust a setting in the Management Client. First go to <strong>Alarms</strong>, then <strong>Alarm Data Settings</strong>. There, select the event properties you want and move them from the left panel to the right.</p>\n<p>To display event properties in the Smart Client, right-click the event header and select which fields to display.</p>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3>4.1 How to Set Up Continuous Recording in Milestone VMS</h3>\n<p>Access the Milestone XProtect Management Client.</p>\n<p>Right-click the Rules tab, then click <strong>Add Rule</strong>.</p>\n<p>Set an appropriate Name, then set the rule description:</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Perform an action in a time interval:</strong> always</li>\n<li><strong>start recording immediately</strong> on All Cameras (or the cameras you want continuously recorded)</li>\n<li><strong>Perform an action when time interval ends:</strong> stop recording immediately, then click <strong>Finish</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>After completing setup, check in Milestone XProtect SmartClient to confirm that all video is being recorded.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Version</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.00</td><td>Initial document.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.10</td><td>Added Section 4, FAQ.</td></tr>\n</table>";
